<p>Candidate for Mayor, Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027</p>
<p><a href="https://www.joeforchicago.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website</a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.joeforchicago.com/priorities" rel="nofollow noopener">Joe Holberg&#39;s campaign lists ten priorities, each with a short statement and a set of key ideas. Tap here to read them on his site, then come back to comment.</a></p>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>The platform</h3>
<p>Economy: Cut red tape for businesses, recruit national and global companies, and train workers for growing fields like quantum, clean energy, and AI.</p>
<p>Budget: Freeze and then lower property taxes, reduce spending, and work with unions and the state on pensions.</p>
<p>Schools and safety: Get chronically absent students back in class. Community policing, violence prevention, mental health crisis teams, and a cleaner, safer CTA.</p>
<p>Growth: Reverse Chicago&#39;s population loss with more visitors, big events, and an easier move for new residents. Build more housing in every neighborhood.</p>
<h3>Next to the other candidates</h3>
<p>Only Holberg: A plan aimed at growing the city&#39;s population.</p>
<p>Taxes: Holberg and Wilson promise lower taxes. Mendoza, Kelly, and Brewer say relief comes from a bigger tax base, and Carlisle proposes a new income tax tied to pension reform.</p>
<p>Mental health: Holberg, Quigley, and Carlisle would send mental health teams to crisis calls. Quigley and Carlisle would also reopen neighborhood mental health clinics.</p>
